   "text": "About **5 years** of driving.\n\n**Fuel math**  \n- Car A: 14,000 mi ÷ 24 mpg ≈ 583 gal/year → 583 × $3.40 ≈ $1,983/year.  \n- Car B: 14,000 mi ÷ 48 mpg ≈ 292 gal/year → 292 × $3.40 ≈ $992/year.  \n- Annual savings = $1,983 – $992 ≈ $991.  \n- Price gap = $27,000 – $22,000 = $5,000.  \n- Break‑even years = $5,000 ÷ $991 ≈ 5.0 years."
